Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: reset PSE on single-PPE SoCs (mt7623)

On the MT7623 (Banana Pi R2) the DSA switch (MT7530) links up and traps
management frames to the CPU, but user ports forward no data - DHCP/ARP
leave the port yet nothing comes back - so the onboard switch is unusable.
A driver re-probe (unbind/bind of mtk_soc_eth) fixes it immediately, which
pins the fault to the frame-engine bring-up, not the switch.

The cause is commit e8716b5b0e2e ("net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: do not reset
PSE when setting FE"), which removed the global PSE reset from mtk_open() to
fix multi-PPE parts (MT7988). On a single-PPE SoC like MT7623 that reset is
required after the switch attaches, otherwise the PSE never enters a state
that forwards DSA-tagged traffic. Re-add it, gated on ppe_num < 2 so the
multi-PPE SoCs the reset was removed for are unaffected.

Verified on a Banana Pi R2: with the reset restored the DSA ports lease DHCP
and route (wan/lan get an address and ping the gateway) from boot, matching
the behaviour a manual driver re-probe produces.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -3619,6 +3619,18 @@
 			mtk_gdm_config(eth, target_mac->id, gdm_config);
 		}
 
+		/* Single-PPE SoCs (e.g. MT7623 / Banana Pi R2) need the global
+		 * PSE reset here for the DSA switch data path to come up after
+		 * boot - without it the user ports link but forward no data
+		 * until the frame engine is re-probed. The reset was dropped
+		 * for multi-PPE parts in commit e8716b5b0e2e ("net: ethernet:
+		 * mtk_eth_soc: do not reset PSE when setting FE"), so gate it
+		 * on ppe_num < 2 where it is required and harmless. */
+		if (eth->soc->ppe_num < 2) {
+			mtk_w32(eth, RST_GL_PSE, MTK_RST_GL);
+			mtk_w32(eth, 0, MTK_RST_GL);
+		}
+
 		napi_enable(&eth->tx_napi);
 		napi_enable(&eth->rx_napi);
 		mtk_tx_irq_enable(eth, MTK_TX_DONE_INT);
